[C1] PASS after limiting, no cell is driven negative by one forward-Euler step: over 4000 random fields the unlimited update goes negative in 4000 of them, worst -5.879e+00; the limited update never does, worst 0.000e+00
[C2] PASS the limiter is inactive exactly where the cell can afford its outflow: 25974 of 25974 cells that can afford their outflow keep theta == 1 bitwise, and 0 cells that cannot were left unlimited; so the high-order flux is untouched away from depletion
[C3] PASS conservation comes from both cells of a face seeing one number, not from the donor rule: on a closed block the limited tendency sums to 1.7e-16 of the flux scale over 2000 fields; a per-cell limiter, where each cell scales only its own outflow, leaks 8.5e-01. The donor rule buys positivity (C1, C7), not conservation: any single factor per face telescopes
[C4] PASS the margin is 4096 ulp in float64 and 64 ulp in float32, for a reason: 4096 ulp of float64 is 9.09e-13 of the cell's gas mass, negligible; the same 4096 ulp in float32 would be 4.88e-04, which the header calls the size of a real repair, so float32 uses 64 ulp = 7.63e-06
[C5] PASS every shipped integrator forms a stage as a convex combination of an old state and one damped full-step Euler update: rk1 alpha max 1.000; rk2 alpha max 1.000; rk3 alpha max 1.000; rk3s4 alpha max 1.000. Each stage is w0 U0 + w1 (U + alpha dU) with w0 + w1 = 1 and alpha = w2/w1 <= 1, so limiting at the full dt keeps the stage non-negative
[C6] PASS the carry withholds exactly the energy and momentum of the mass it withheld, at the same face and from the same donor: max |energy removed - (unscaled minus scaled) mass times donor enthalpy| = 1.8e-15; same for momentum 8.9e-16, over 2000 faces sets
[C7] PASS each face is scaled by the factor of the cell it drains, not of its own index: 46000 interior faces checked against the donor rule, 0 mismatches; the donor is the lower cell where the flux is positive and the upper otherwise
7/7 claims pass
